  description: 'An emergency contraceptive designed to prevent pregnancy after unprotected
    sex or contraceptive failure. It is typically an oral pill/tablet containing
    levonorgestrel, a synthetic hormone that prevents or delays ovulation. It reduces
    the risk of pregnancy when taken within 72 hours of unprotected sex, with the
    effectiveness decreasing over time. It should only be used as an emergency contraceptive. '
  usageInstruction: "It is important to note that Plan B has been reported to be
    less effective for individuals weighing over 155\u2013165 lbs (70\u201375 kg)
    or with a BMI over 30. "
